rTest.kt** - Added 4 comprehensive tests:\n   - Tests the core confirmation flow (CREATED → CONFIRMED)\n   - Tests idempotency (CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED)\n   - Tests error case for CANCELLED shipment (409)\n   - Tests error case for non-existent shipment (404)\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n**Requirement:**\nAdd a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that moves a shipment from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED` status, handles idempotency, and rejects attempts to confirm cancelled or non-existent shipments with appropriate HTTP status codes.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt` - Added `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` error code to support consistent error responses when confirming cancelled shipments\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` - Added `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` endpoint implementing the confirmation logic with proper error handling and idempotency\n- `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Added 4 tests covering the core functionality, idempotency, and error cases\n\n**Tests:**\n- `confirms a CREATED shipment and moves it to CONFIRMED` - Verifies state transition from CREATED to CONFIRMED status\n- `confirm is idempotent for an already CONFIRMED shipment` - Verifies calling confirm twice succeeds both times with no change\n- `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with conflict` - Verifies 409 response with correct error code\n- `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404` - Verifies 404 response with correct error code\n\n**Verification:**\nCommand: `cd sample-service && ./mvnw test`\nResult: BUILD SUCCESS with 17 tests passing (9 ShipmentControllerTest including 4 new tests, 4 OrderControllerTest, 3 CustomerControllerTest, 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests)\n\n**Not done:**\nNothing. All acceptance criteria have been satisfied, all tests pass, and the implementation follows the existing code conventions and error handling patterns."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":784,"cache_read_input_tokens":25118,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":784},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5f4cc45-03f1-4812-afc5-8194131e3c45","uuid":"6da6be0e-4143-4b15-8efc-3788ef4c4e8d","timestamp":"2026-09-30T11:38:40.786Z","request_id":"req_011CfZZLVCtLSsL6wnz1q4vL"}
